.TH WEB-TRX 1 "2026" "pluto-tx" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
web-trx \- start, stop and query the Web-TRX browser interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B web-trx
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B web-trx
\fBstart\fR|\fBstop\fR|\fBrestart\fR|\fBstatus\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBlog\fR|\fBservice enable\fR|\fBservice disable\fR
.PP
controls the Web-TRX server (default https://<host>:8321). The login password is generated on the first start and kept in ~/.config/pluto-tx/web-trx.env.
\fBservice enable\fR sets it up as a system service for headless operation (starts at boot without login) \- a deliberate step, as the station can then transmit without anybody logged in.
.PP
Run
.B web-trx \-\-help
for all options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/pluto-tx
program code
.TP
.I /usr/lib/pluto-tx
bundled native components (gr-m17, gr-lora_sdr, rade_c, ft8_lib, js8ref)
.TP
.I ~/.config/pluto-tx/web-trx.env
Web-TRX settings (password, port, TLS)
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/web-trx/
Web-TRX runtime data (log, PID, TLS certificate, sessions, TX log)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pluto-tx (1),
.BR pluto-advanced-rx (1),
.BR pluto-cli (1),
.BR web-trx (1),
.BR pluto-tx-doctor (1)
.PP
